# Copy to app/.env.local (git ignores it). Expo reads it when you run `npm run web` / `npm start` in app/, and the API
# routes under src/app/v1 read it on the server side. Names only here: never commit a value.
#
# ---- Enough to run everything locally (sign-in, search, capture, lists) -------------------------------------------
NODE_ENV=development
# Sign-in without an email service: the code every email sign-in accepts. Any 6 digits. Development only: the server
# refuses to start with it when NODE_ENV is production.
SECONDHAND_DEV_CODE=
# Where accounts, captures and photos are kept between restarts. Without it they live in memory and vanish on restart.
SECONDHAND_DATA_DIR=
#
# ---- The chat ("What's selling and why") ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One of these. Without either, the chat answers "unavailable" and everything else still works.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# ---- Search reach ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloud browser for the sites read through a real browser (eBay). Without it those sources say they could not be read.
BROWSER_USE_API_KEY=
# Sold prices for valuations and the chat's sold-price tool: the sites read live, comma separated (e.g. poshmark).
SECONDHAND_LIVE_SITES=
# Google Shopping results and, in capture, Google Lens (only when tag, label and barcode reads abstain). Paid per call.
TREG_TOKEN=
# Facebook Marketplace through Apify, for pricing a shown range only.
APIFY_TOKEN=
# eBay's official API, when the app has its own eBay developer keys.
EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Mercari needs a local Chrome to link a browser (path to chrome.exe or the Chrome app binary).
SECONDHAND_CHROME=
#
# ---- Email sign-in on a real host -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RESEND_API_KEY=
SECONDHAND_EMAIL_FROM=
#
# ---- Databricks (the market tables, Genie) --------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABRICKS_HOST=https://your-workspace.cloud.databricks.com
DATABRICKS_TOKEN=
DATABRICKS_WAREHOUSE_ID=your-sql-warehouse-id
#
# ---- Hosted only (set as host secrets, not here) --------------------------------------------------------------------
# DECISION_SIGNING_KEY, SECONDHAND_VAULT_KEY, SECONDHAND_VISITOR_KEY: development makes and keeps its own.
